Subject: [PATCH 19/24] Review sticky-failure tests; leave repros of unrecorded
 write failures

TornWalAppend: a refused write after a failure is either the write-failure
refusal or, after a safepoint's failed I/O, the closed engine's error; only
acknowledged commits are counted either way. TornSlotRewrite: the waiting
commit's refusal carries the recorded failure. WalTransactionBoundary:
reworded the teardown assertion. ReadOnlyAfterWriteFailure.AssertReported:
a null file is not checked (existing callers keep working).

Left failing (suspected engine defects):
- a safepoint's failed WAL append (disk full) is not recorded, so the
  engine stays closed and reads throw (EngineState.Handle);
- a commit's failed WAL append records no file;
- an encrypted WAL preamble sync that cannot sync (UnauthorizedAccess)
  is not recorded, so reads throw.

